Reuse-distance hooks for PHP 5.0.0's Zend allocator (docs/plans/2026-11-15-php-reuse-distance.md).
Every hook is behind EXP_REUSE_GAP: without it the five macros expand to nothing. The hooks
record the block header, the address Zend itself works with, at _emalloc's two hand-outs
(AG(cache) and malloc), _efree, _efree's free to malloc, a successful _erealloc and request
shutdown's frees. They sit away from the nested layer's seven substitutions, whose patch still
applies to the hooked file at fuzz 0 (build.sh checks it).

